Valve material in this repository
---------------------------------

These test fixtures are synthetic images built from hero portraits served by
the game's public image CDN. They exist only to test the photo reader:

- api/testdata/photos/synthetic-*.jpg (rendered by
  scripts/fixtures/make_fixtures.py)
- web/e2e/fixtures/pick-photo.jpg

api/internal/photo/testdata/endscreen.jpg and web/e2e/fixtures/end-screen.jpg
are drawn text only (hero names and numbers, rendered by
scripts/fixtures/make_endscreen.py). The other e2e images are plain gradients.

At runtime the web app loads hero portraits, item images and other artwork
from the game's public image CDN (cdn.cloudflare.steamstatic.com), at the
paths dotaconstants lists. The item art is Valve Corporation's; it is not
redistributed here, and an item whose image fails to load shows its initial.

Data sources
------------

Game data is synced at runtime into the operator's database; none of it is
bundled with the code.

- dotaconstants, https://github.com/odota/dotaconstants
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2017 The OpenDota Project.
  Hero ids, slugs, images, items and patches.
- OpenDota API, https://www.opendota.com / https://docs.opendota.com
  Hero stats, matchups and item popularity. Data provided by OpenDota; use is
  subject to the OpenDota API terms (https://www.opendota.com/api-keys).
- The game's public data feed on dota2.com (datafeed endpoints), operated by
  Valve Corporation. Hero details, abilities, talents and patch notes.

